{"slug":"forza-horizon","title":"Forza Horizon","desc":"Xbox 360, Playground Games 2012 (USA)","notes":["Made with the Forza importer (import_forza.py, a Blender plugin) from the game's own car archives.  Parts are the game's own names (body, bumperFa, hooda, glassLF, headlightL, interior, wheelLF ...) as children of ONE root node named like the archive; the stock car is visible.","BODY KITS (Forza Motorsport 1 / 2 / 4, Forza Horizon): every upgrade part of the shop is in the FBX, HIDDEN, at its place on the car, in Variants/<slot> (bumperF, bumperR, skirtL, skirtR, wing, hood, cage, exhaust, trunk): the game names them <part><letter>, 'a' = stock, b .. t = the tuner kits, race = the race kit.  To see them: <car>_kits.fbx = the stock car and one complete car per kit letter (the kit's parts replace the stock ones), all VISIBLE, in rows of 6.  Variants/driver = the driver mannequin (Forza 1), Variants/popup_up = pop-up lamps up.","LODs: every lower level of detail of every part (LOD2-LOD5; Forza 4 / Horizon: LOD1-LOD5 next to the LOD0 car) is HIDDEN in LODs/LOD<n>.","Left out: skeleton, locators, blur discs.  Body paint is a run time shader in all these games: one plain red (the stock paint of the first livery in Forza Motorsport), baked ambient occlusion is NOT in the FBX (it is in the plugin and in the renders).","The front of the car is +Z like in the other games; the car stands on the ground at y = 0.","Same car format as Forza Motorsport 4 (180 archives).  The 15 traffic cars (VW Beetle 04, Prius, Camry, Corolla, RAV4, PT Cruiser, Durango, Yukon XL, Taurus SHO, A4 Avant, XC70, Leaf, Express van, Kenworth T440, tour bus) have no LOD0 model in the game: their lod0 / cockpit files hold placeholders (tiny quads or one 20 cm box per part), so these cars are the game's LOD1, the best model there is.  No car of this game or of Forza Motorsport 4 has an engine model (no section or material of an engine in any file); Forza Horizon 6 cars have one (engine_a, engineBay_a).","RIMS: _Rims holds every file of media/wheels (290 zips; the 7 'Tire*' files are tyres only and left out): the LOD0 rim and the LOD1 tyre as two objects.  A few wheels (buses, trucks, the Taurus SHO, the A4 Avant) have only a stub at LOD0: their rim is the LOD1 model.  The LOD0 rim is fitted to the size of its LOD1 model (272 of the 290; the bounds in the file header, which stretch the vertices, are those of rim + tyre: the rim would be 30 % too big)."],"tags":["forza-horizon"],"sections":[{"key":"cars","label":"Cars","items":[["alf_8c_08","",20693609,"forza-horizon","car-alf_8c_08.zip","thumbs/forza-horizon/cars/car-alf_8c_08.webp"],["asc_kz1r_12","",20623637,"forza-horizon","car-asc_kz1r_12.zip","thumbs/forza-horizon/cars/car-asc_kz1r_12.webp"],["ast_db5vantage_64","",19937459,"forza-horizon","car-ast_db5vantage_64.zip","thumbs/forza-horizon/cars/car-ast_db5vantage_64.webp"],["ast_dbr1_58","",20799201,"forza-horizon","car-ast_dbr1_58.zip","thumbs/forza-horizon/cars/car-ast_dbr1_58.webp"],["ast_one77_10","",18795788,"forza-horizon","car-ast_one77_10.zip","thumbs/forza-horizon/cars/car-ast_one77_10.webp"],["ast_v12zagato_12","",22944502,"forza-horizon","car-ast_v12zagato_12.zip","thumbs/forza-horizon/cars/car-ast_v12zagato_12.webp"],["ast_virage_12","",19207491,"forza-horizon","car-ast_virage_12.zip","thumbs/forza-horizon/cars/car-ast_virage_12.webp"],["aud_a4avant_04","",2249252,"forza-horizon","car-aud_a4avant_04.zip","thumbs/forza-horizon/cars/car-aud_a4avant_04.webp"],["aud_r8gt_11","",23694307,"forza-horizon","car-aud_r8gt_11.zip","thumbs/forza-horizon/cars/car-aud_r8gt_11.webp"],["aud_r8gtspyder_12","",24746153,"forza-horizon","car-aud_r8gtspyder_12.zip","thumbs/forza-horizon/cars/car-aud_r8gtspyder_12.webp"],["aud_rs4_06","",21669477,"forza-horizon","car-aud_rs4_06.zip","thumbs/forza-horizon/cars/car-aud_rs4_06.webp"],["aud_sportquattro_83","",20965265,"forza-horizon","car-aud_sportquattro_83.zip","thumbs/forza-horizon/cars/car-aud_sportquattro_83.webp"],["a